-- id: exp6868-three-family-semantic-scoring-stream-v2
-  title: Three-family semantic contrast scoring stream v2
-  track: verification
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: codex
-  model: gpt-5.6-sol
-  requires_gpu: true
-  max_turns: 50
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 600
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.09.601
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6868_three_family_semantic_scoring_stream_v2.json
-  gated_on:
-    - upstream: exp6867-tokenizer-aware-semantic-preregistration-v2
-      artifact_field: semantic_contrast_preregistration_v2_ready_score
-      op: '=='
-      value: 1
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    Exp6851 produced raw fixed-sequence scores but its semantic claim was not identifiable. Exp6864
-    never ran because its tokenizer prerequisite failed. Exp6867 supplies a new, canonical-tokenizer
-    bound, nuisance-matched, preregistered stream. This task produces raw scores only. It trains no
-    text scorer, generates no candidate answer, and does not reopen the retired Phase-D external
-    generated-text scorer lane.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    MODEL_SPECS:
-    - unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF (flagship MoE)
-    - unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF (flagship dense)
-    - unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF (middle MoE)
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
-    - {project_root}/ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml, phase_d_external_text_scorer entry
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6850_three_family_scoring_admission_canary.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6851_three_family_isomorphic_compatibility_stream.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6864_three_family_semantic_contrast_scoring_stream.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6867_tokenizer_aware_semantic_preregistration_v2.json
-    - {project_root}/scripts/experiment_template.py, cached_sota_pair() pattern
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/inference/llama_cpp_process.py
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/llm-ebm-inference/spec.md
-
-    TASK:
-    Run local llama.cpp CUDA forced-sequence scoring for every frozen eligible calibration and held
-    cell in every MODEL_SPEC. Preserve token-level receipts, checkpoints, process ownership, and
-    nuisance identities. Hide exact labels from model processes and make no semantic-effect claim.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: call cached_sota_pair(); require
-       semantic_contrast_preregistration_v2_ready_score=1, exact model and canonical tokenizer
-       hashes, CUDA token scoring, sufficient disk, task-owned ports, and a bounded GPU lease.
-       Observe but never interrupt unrelated processes. On failure, write
-       complete_blocked_three_family_semantic_scoring_stream_v2 with gate_check_summary.
-    1. Add REQ-INFERENCE-6868 and tests first. Cover lease loss, stale PID, occupied port, hash
-       drift, label exposure, NaN, timeout, partial checkpoint, restart, and owned teardown.
-    2. Run one model process at a time. Record command, PID, PID start ticks, ownership token, model
-       and tokenizer hashes, GPU UUID, visible devices, offload, port, context, and VRAM samples.
-    3. Score exact frozen prompt-plus-candidate sequences. Store token IDs, token log probabilities,
-       finite checks, raw sum, per-token normalization, latency, sequence hash, group identity, and
-       nuisance-transform identity.
-    4. Generate no answers, repairs, labels, or judgments. Model inputs must not contain semantic
-       labels. Record generated_answer_count=0 and held_label_access_count=0.
-    5. Keep calibration and held score sidecars separately hashed. The task may write scores but
-       must not reduce held effects.
-    6. Checkpoint atomically after every model and bounded group batch. Verify input hashes before
-       resume and rerun only incomplete cells. Preserve failed and timeout cells without imputation.
-    7. Tear down only task-owned processes. Record port release and process exit.
-    8. Set semantic_contrast_stream_v2_complete_score=1 only when every required model cell or
-       explicit failure row exists, raw receipts verify, checkpoints are complete, and teardown is
-       clean. Stream completion is not a scientific positive.
-    9. Run focused tests, ruff, OpenSpec coverage, adversarial verification, artifact-convention
-       audit, verdict-row consistency lint, CUDA-authenticity checks, and root-clutter checks.
-    10. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles; preconditions_checked;
-       inference_substrate (live local llama.cpp CUDA forced-sequence scoring); duration_s;
-       model_specs (all three exact MODEL_SPECS); models_used; missing_model_manifest;
-       model_artifact_hashes; tokenizer_receipts; process_receipts; accelerator_samples;
